// R3 instrument 1 (2026-07-16; doc 15 §1): the eviction/refault LEDGER.
//
// Captures the two filemap tracepoints (per-page add/delete from the page
// cache, carrying inode + page offset) plus the vmscan reclaim begin/end
// tracepoints for batch context — emitting a machine-parseable
//   <ns> <event> <ino> <pgoff> <slab_tag>
// stream, filtered IN-PROBE to ONLY shard slabs (the event rate on unrelated
// files would swamp the perf ring). The shard inode set is a BODY fragment
// (generated by r3_inode_map.py into _r3_inode_body.bt); r3_splice_probes.py
// line-anchors it into this probe's single BEGIN at the /*INODE_BODY*/.
//
// Events (since REQ-3h, 2026-07-16):
//   ADD   — filemap:mm_filemap_add_to_page_cache  (a page faulted INTO cache)
//   DEL   — filemap:mm_filemap_delete_from_page_cache (a page evicted)
// (RBEG/REND/SHRINK vmscan batch-context events DROPPED — see the note at the
//  reclaim-context section below; they had no page index to downsample, were
//  95% of 12g volume, and the join never keyed on them. Reclaim pressure is
//  in per_pass.cg_delta pgscan/pgsteal, not the ledger.)
//
// The ADD/DEL pair is the residue-vs-repeat-set sort, page by page: DEL =
// kernel evicted, ADD = page came back (fault). Joined to the per-query extent
// map on (ino, pgoff→extent) and sliced by the driver's pass-boundary
// CLOCK_MONOTONIC ns timestamps → R3's per-page × per-query attribution.
//
// DOWNSAMPLE (fixed 2026-07-16 after the REQ-3f 92% perf-ring loss): the first
// live run printf'd PER PAGE EVENT — the cold-fill fault storm faults ~4M
// pages → ~4M printf calls through the default perf ring → "Lost N events"
// summed to 3.9M (91.7% loss, busted the ≤1% §R3 bar). doc 15 §4 anticipated
// this: "Fail → downsample (e.g. pgoff sampling) and rerun." This probe
// samples ONE PAGE PER EXTENT: the ADD/DEL predicates gate on
// `args->index % 512 == 0` — extent = 2 MiB = 512 pages, and page index 0 of
// every extent is always a 512-multiple, so this fires exactly once per
// touched extent (readahead touches contiguous ranges from the extent start,
// so the boundary page of a touched extent IS touched). 512× volume reduction
// → drop rate → ~0%, the per-event TSV format + ns are PRESERVED (the join is
// unchanged), and pgoff is extent-aligned so pgoff_to_extent is exact. The
// only loss: extents whose boundary page was never faulted (rare under
// readahead) — acceptable since the query-extent map (instrument 5) is itself
// extent-granular and the join attributes at that granularity anyway.
//
// Drops: perf-buffer overrun is counted and printed at exit (the §R3 bar is
// ≤1% drop rate; over → that cell's ledger is INVALID, never quoted).
// Output is TSV to stdout for machine parsing (r3_join_analysis.py).

BEGIN
{
// AUTO-GENERATED by r3_inode_map.py — bpftrace BODY fragment
// (NOT a BEGIN block). Spliced into each probe's single BEGIN at the
// /*INODE_BODY*/ placeholder by the orchestrator. Populates
// @shard_inodes[ino] = <tag> so the probes filter filemap/vmscan
// events to ONLY shard slabs IN-PROBE.
// generated 2026-07-16; scope=forward; 8 inodes.
  @shard_inodes[68116944364127856] = 1;
  @shard_inodes[1970324837232434] = 1;
  @shard_inodes[1407374883811123] = 1;
  @shard_inodes[1407374883811027] = 1;
  @shard_inodes[1407374883811050] = 1;
  @shard_inodes[10977524091987289] = 1;
  @shard_inodes[37717646879500707] = 1;
  @shard_inodes[8444249301592441] = 1;
  @shard_inodes_count = 8;
  // breadcrumb: count how many shard inodes the spliced body populated.
  // A host run prints this within seconds of attach — if it is 0, the inode
  // map did NOT load (cross-container inode remap) and the cell should be
  // killed before it burns ~1h producing no events.
  printf("LEDGER_START ts=%llu shard_inodes_loaded=%llu\n", nsecs, @shard_inodes_count);
}

// ── per-page add (fault into cache) — SAMPLED 1-per-extent ────────────────
// KERNEL FIELD NAMES (fixed 2026-07-16): the filemap tracepoints' shared event
// class mm_filemap_op_page_cache (include/trace/events/filemap.h) exposes the
// inode as `args->i_ino` (NOT `args->ino` — that field does not exist → probe
// fails to attach → zero events). The page offset is `args->index`. Both ADD
// and DEL inherit the same TP_STRUCT__entry, so DEL carries the page offset
// too. The `args->index % 512 == 0` gate samples the extent boundary page.
tracepoint:filemap:mm_filemap_add_to_page_cache
/@shard_inodes[args->i_ino] && args->index % 512 == 0/
{
  @emitted_add++;
  printf("%llu\tADD\t%llu\t%llu\t%d\n", nsecs, args->i_ino, args->index, @shard_inodes[args->i_ino]);
}

// ── per-page delete (eviction) — SAMPLED 1-per-extent ─────────────────────
tracepoint:filemap:mm_filemap_delete_from_page_cache
/@shard_inodes[args->i_ino] && args->index % 512 == 0/
{
  @emitted_del++;
  printf("%llu\tDEL\t%llu\t%llu\t%d\n", nsecs, args->i_ino, args->index, @shard_inodes[args->i_ino]);
}

// ── reclaim batch context: DROPPED 2026-07-16 (REQ-3h fix for REQ-3g's 12g drop)
// The three vmscan tracepoints (RBEG = mm_vmscan_memcg_reclaim_begin, REND =
// _end, SHRINK = mm_vmscan_lru_shrink_inactive) were REMOVED. They carry NO
// page index, so the `% 512` extent-downsample (the REQ-3f perf-ring fix)
// CAN'T gate them — they fire per-batch-event regardless. At 12g (the
// reclaim-storm cap) they were 95% of ledger volume (138,943 RBEG + 138,850
// REND + 164,280 SHRINK = 442k vs 22,897 ADD/DEL), overrunning the perf ring
// to drop_rate=0.118 (busting the §R3 ≤1% bar, 12g ledger INVALID).
// The join (r3_join_analysis.py) keys ONLY on ADD/DEL (the per-page
// attribution stream); RBEG/REND/SHRINK were never join inputs — pure buffer
// pressure with zero attribution value. Removing them cuts 12g volume ~21× →
// drop→~0%, ADD/DEL unchanged and still extent-aligned.
// The reclaim-PRESSURE signal they gestured at is ALREADY captured at pass
// granularity by the driver's per_pass.cg_delta (cgroup-v2 pgscan/pgsteal
// deltas — the 04-doc §2.2 pressure-scaled clock, in the cell JSON, not the
// ledger). Cap-grading came from pass boundaries, not these per-batch events,
// so no information the join consumed is lost — only a firehose that served no
// join purpose. (The 16g cell's banked ledger, captured BEFORE this drop,
// had drop=0 anyway because 16g doesn't reclaim-storm — it is unaffected and
// stays the artifact of record; this probe change applies to the 12g re-run.)

END
{
  // emitted_add/del = sampled events written; bpftrace's own "Lost N events"
  // exit summary is the §R3 drop-rate bar (≤1%). Past-END lines may be absent
  // (the tracer is docker-stop'd before detach — the verifier falls back to
  // counting the event lines directly).
  printf("LEDGER_END ts=%llu emitted_add=%llu emitted_del=%llu\n", nsecs, @emitted_add, @emitted_del);
}
